---
title: Green Mole with Chayote
cooklang: 2
servings: 4
cuisine: Mexican
source: recipe-pack dinner-2/4407-green-mole-3
---

= Chayote -> roasted chayote

`Preheat 220 °C` the #oven{} to 220 °C. `Cut` @chayotes{4}(peeled) in half on a #board{}, `scoop` out
the pits and `cut` each half into three spears.

`Toss` the @&chayotes{} with @olive oil{2%tbsp} and @salt{1%tsp} in a #bowl{}. -> coated chayote

`Spread` the @&coated chayote{} on a #baking sheet{} lined with #parchment{}.

`Roast` for ~oven{50-60%minutes} until ~{tender and richly browned}, then `sprinkle` with
@cilantro{10%g}(chopped).

= Mole verde -> mole

`Roast` @poblano chile{1} on a #+baking sheet{} under the #broiler{}, turning, until ~{the skin is blistered and blackened}; `cool`, `peel` off the skin, `remove the seeds` and stem, `rinse` and
`chop` roughly.

`Scoop` the @&poblano chile{} into a #blender{}.

`Simmer` @tomatillos{450%g}(husked, halved), @garlic{4%cloves}(halved) and @white onion{1}(roughly
chopped) with @water{500%ml} and @salt{1%tsp} in a #saucepan{} for ~{10%minutes} until ~{the tomatillos lose their bright green colour}. -> tomatillo pot

`Scoop` the @&tomatillos{}, the @&garlic{} and the @&white onion{} with a #slotted spoon{} into
the #&blender{}; the cooking liquid stays behind.

`Add` @sesame seeds{50%g}, @pumpkin seeds{70%g}(toasted), @mixed herbs{40%g}(parsley, cilantro,
epazote), @cumin{1/4%tsp}(ground), @black pepper{1/2%tsp}(ground) and @Mexican oregano{1%tsp} to
the #&blender{} and `blend` until ~{smooth}. -> purée

`Heat medium` @&olive oil{1%tbsp} in a large #+saucepan{} over medium heat, `add` the @&purée{} all at
once and `stir` nearly continuously as it reduces and thickens, ~{7%minutes}.

`Add` the @&tomatillo pot{350%ml}, partially `cover` and `simmer medium-low` over medium-low heat for
~{20%minutes}, stirring regularly. `Season` with @&salt{2%tsp}.

= Finish the dish

`Rewarm` the @&roasted chayote{} in the #&oven{}, `divide` the @&roasted chayote{} between warm
#plates{} and `spoon` the @&mole{} over. `Strew` with @?pumpkin seeds{}(crushed) and `serve`.
